\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Putting event masses on a common scale}
\date{2026-11-10}

\p{The Gaussian normalization theorem \ref{fdip-002T} gives a finite
positive value for the integral of #{w_Q}. To compare events in the
field space, their masses need a common scale. How can this integral
normalize #{w_Q} to a Borel probability measure?}
